web/node_modules
bin/
tmp/
*.log

# Runtime territory. The quickstart bind-mounts docker/hearth and
# docker/config, and the daemon writes root-owned state through them:
# keys.json/keys.lock/tokens.json (0600), sessions/, memory/, the
# sideband socket, the custos/ vault dir (0700 — the context walker
# cannot even open it), nuntius/ inboxes, backup.lock, .setup-done.
# Any one of them kills the next `docker compose up --build` with
# "checking context: no permission to read ...". Ignoring the two bind
# roots ends the whack-a-mole: the image COPYes nothing from either
# (Dockerfile takes Go source + web/; config and persona land at
# runtime via the mounts).
docker/hearth/
docker/config/
